# =============================================================================
#  HMC-CEC.orch - MPAI Communicating Entities in Context (HMC-CEC V2.2)
#  Workflow Description Language v0.3, AIF V3.0
#
#  One Controller, one Module. The User Agent offers the Controller data
#  identified by Data Type and Port Number, and asks for data identified the
#  same way. It names no AIM.
#
#  The Module is Communicating Entities in Context: the person (an Entity in a
#  real or virtual context) shows the face and speaks or types; the Machine
#  understands the person and the context (Multimodal Frontend Description,
#  Entity and Context Understanding), translates where the person speaks
#  another language (Text and Speech Translation), answers (Entity Dialogue
#  Processing, Text-to-Text Translation) and gives its Portable Avatar. The
#  Selector of each turn says the input medium (text or speech) and the
#  languages: the one the person speaks and the one of the answer.
#
#  Made 2026-11-25 (N-50 e) as the workflow of CPS, with the Module of HMC.
# =============================================================================

workflow HMC-CEC over 1HMC-CEC-V2.2-I01

on Start:

    ask Controller to start

    prompt "Communicating Entities in Context: show your face and talk with me; I understand you and where you are, and I answer in the language you chose."

    loop until Stop:

        acquire Face (OSD-BVO-V1.5)
        acquire UserAudio (OSD-BAO-V1.5) via VAD
             or UserText  (OSD-BTO-V1.5)
        acquire TurnSelector (OSD-SEL-V1.5)

        offer Face (OSD-BVO-V1.5:1)
        branch on UserText {
            offer UserText (OSD-BTO-V1.5:1)
        } else {
            offer UserAudio (OSD-BAO-V1.5:1)
        }
        offer TurnSelector (OSD-SEL-V1.5:1)
        offer MachineID (string:1) = "MPAI as a Service"
        ask   MachinePortableAvatar (PAF-PAV-V1.6)
        present MachinePortableAvatar

on Stop:

    ask Controller to stop
